{"type":"assistant","uuid":"870320e1-d830-4c7d-9419-b4b382d72847","session_id":"5effc2e7-6d69-447d-8a49-a66d3777c03d","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"870320e1-d830-4c7d-9419-b4b382d72847","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to fix a bug in an Android project where entering too large numbers in manual entry dialogs causes a crash. Let me start by understanding the bug and locating the relevant code.\n\nFrom the bug description:\n1. TOTP Period/Digits crash: `NumberFormatException: For input string: \"3000000000\"` at `ManualEntryDialog.java:293`\n2. HOTP Counter crash: `NumberFormatException: For input string: \"1000000000000000000000\"` at `ManualEntryDialog.java:245`\n\nThe issue is that:\n- Period and Digits fields parse as `Integer.parseInt()` but can accept values > Integer.MAX_VALUE\n- Counter field parses as `Long.parseLong()` but can accept values > Long.MAX_VALUE\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
