{"type":"assistant","uuid":"97fbcf4e-950f-4e77-82c6-910840c1ed7b","session_id":"5effc2e7-6d69-447d-8a49-a66d3777c03d","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"97fbcf4e-950f-4e77-82c6-910840c1ed7b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe patch applies cleanly and produces the correct output. Here's the complete summary:\n\n---\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**File:** `app/src/src/main/java/org/shadowice/flocke/andotp/Dialogs/ManualEntryDialog.java`\n\n### Root Cause\nThe `ManualEntryDialog` used `Integer.parseInt()` and `Long.parseLong()` directly on user input without validating that the values fit within their respective type ranges. When a user enters a number exceeding `Integer.MAX_VALUE` (2,147,483,647) in the Period/Digits fields, or a number exceeding `Long.MAX_VALUE` (9,223,372,036,854,775,807) in the Counter field, these methods either throw `NumberFormatException` or silently wrap the value — both causing crashes.\n\n### Fix Applied\n\n**Added two safe parsing helpers:**\n- `tryParseInt(String text, int[] result)` — parses as `int` but also verifies the value round-trips correctly, catching overflow inputs like `\"3000000000\"` where `Integer.parseInt` silently wraps.\n- `tryParseLong(String text, long[] result)` — same for `long` values.\n\n**Two layers of protection:**\n1. **TextWatcher `afterTextChanged()`** — uses safe parsing to disable the Save button immediately when an out-of-range value is detected. This is the primary defense.\n2. **Save button `onClick` handler** — uses the same safe parsing as a safety net, returning early if parsing fails (the button should never be enabled with invalid data, but this prevents crashes if it somehow is).\n\n### Patch Location\nThe patch is available at `/tmp/fix-crash-large-number.patch` and can be applied with:\n```bash\ncd /path/to/project && patch -p1 < /tmp/fix-crash-large-number.patch\n```\n\n### Testing Verification\nThe helper methods were independently verified with the exact crash inputs:\n- `\"3000000000\"` → `false` (was the TOTP Period crash input)\n- `\"1000000000000000000000\"` → `false` (was the HOTP Counter crash input)\n- `\"30\"` → `true, 30` (valid input, works correctly)\n- `\"2147483647\"` → `true, 2147483647` (Integer.MAX_VALUE, edge case handled)\n- `\"9223372036854775807\"` → `true, 9223372036854775807` (Long.MAX_VALUE, edge case handled)"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":59754,"output_tokens":634,"cache_read_input_tokens":58688,"total_tokens":60388}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"69e004df-d2cc-4f0e-877f-04b127284240","session_id":"5effc2e7-6d69-447d-8a49-a66d3777c03d","is_error":false,"duration_ms":421929,"duration_api_ms":168798,"num_turns":34,"result":"\n\nThe patch applies cleanly and produces the correct output. Here's the complete summary:\n\n---\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**File:** `app/src/src/main/java/org/shadowice/flocke/andotp/Dialogs/ManualEntryDialog.java`\n\n### Root Cause\nThe `ManualEntryDialog` used `Integer.parseInt()` and `Long.parseLong()` directly on user input without validating that the values fit within their respective type ranges. When a user enters a number exceeding `Integer.MAX_VALUE` (2,147,483,647) in the Period/Digits fields, or a number exceeding `Long.MAX_VALUE` (9,223,372,036,854,775,807) in the Counter field, these methods either throw `NumberFormatException` or silently wrap the value — both causing crashes.\n\n### Fix Applied\n\n**Added two safe parsing helpers:**\n- `tryParseInt(String text, int[] result)` — parses as `int` but also verifies the value round-trips correctly, catching overflow inputs like `\"3000000000\"` where `Integer.parseInt` silently wraps.\n- `tryParseLong(String text, long[] result)` — same for `long` values.\n\n**Two layers of protection:**\n1. **TextWatcher `afterTextChanged()`** — uses safe parsing to disable the Save button immediately when an out-of-range value is detected. This is the primary defense.\n2. **Save button `onClick` handler** — uses the same safe parsing as a safety net, returning early if parsing fails (the button should never be enabled with invalid data, but this prevents crashes if it somehow is).\n\n### Patch Location\nThe patch is available at `/tmp/fix-crash-large-number.patch` and can be applied with:\n```bash\ncd /path/to/project && patch -p1 < /tmp/fix-crash-large-number.patch\n```\n\n### Testing Verification\nThe helper methods were independently verified with the exact crash inputs:\n- `\"3000000000\"` → `false` (was the TOTP Period crash input)\n- `\"1000000000000000000000\"` → `false` (was the HOTP Counter crash input)\n- `\"30\"` → `true, 30` (valid input, works correctly)\n- `\"2147483647\"` → `true, 2147483647` (Integer.MAX_VALUE, edge case handled)\n- `\"9223372036854775807\"` → `true, 9223372036854775807` (Long.MAX_VALUE, edge case handled)","usage":{"input_tokens":1470452,"output_tokens":15256,"cache_read_input_tokens":1389648,"total_tokens":1485708},"permission_denials":[]}
